@startuml
title Lifecycle of a Rholang-Authored Language Specification
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #334155
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #64748B

participant "Rholang\nprocess" as P #E0E7FF
participant "spec value\n<latex>v</latex>" as V #E0E7FF
participant "elaborator\n<latex>\mathcal{E}</latex>\n**G1**" as E #A7F3D0
participant "validator\n<latex>\mathcal{V}</latex>\n**G2**" as VAL #A7F3D0
participant "identity\n<latex>\mathcal{F}</latex>" as FP #FBCFE8
participant "versioned\nregistry" as REG #DDD6FE
participant "backend\ngenerators" as BE #DCFCE7
participant "RSpace /\nFLT resolver" as RS #BFDBFE

== 1. Construction (pure — no COMM) ==
P -> V : build nested Map / List / Tuple / String literals
note right of V #E0E7FF
  Constructing a spec is **value construction**: no send,
  no receive, no name creation (§III.9). COMM is Rholang's
  communication event — the rendezvous of a send with a
  matching receive on the same channel. Two processes
  building the same spec produce **equal** values, hence
  equal fingerprints, hence identical machinery.
end note

== 2. Elaboration and validation (fail-closed) ==
P -> E : <latex>\mathcal{E}(v)</latex>
E -> E : canonicalize (§III.5), then gate the notation\nversion, the top-level key set, and every tag's arity
E --> P : <latex>\texttt{Err(SpecError)}</latex> on any malformed node,\ncarrying the **value path** at which it failed
E -> VAL : <latex>\texttt{LanguageDef}</latex>
VAL -> VAL : composition, then the **reserved-label fence**,\nthen ""validate_language"", auto-injection,\nstratification
note right of VAL #A7F3D0
  ★ The name-and-label fence runs **AFTER composition**, not first.
  ""extends"" / ""includes"" / ""mixins"" pull in a base language's whole
  vocabulary, ""exports { A => B }"" renames a category to an arbitrary
  string, and ""replacements"" mints a fresh label — so a gate on the
  raw value would never see three of the ways a reserved name arrives.
  The predicate is a **prefix**: a label is reserved iff it starts
  with ""^"" (§IX.5.1).
end note
VAL --> P : <latex>\texttt{Err(ValidationError)}</latex> with a **value path**,\nnot a Rust ""Span""

== 3. Identity ==
VAL -> FP : augmented <latex>\texttt{LanguageDef}</latex>
FP -> FP : <latex>\mathcal{F} = \texttt{mettail-langdef-v2:}\;\mathrm{blake3}(\mathrm{ident}(d))</latex>
note right of FP #FBCFE8
  Frontend-independent by construction: <latex>\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{E}(v))</latex> equals
  <latex>\mathcal{F}(\texttt{reconstruct\_language\_def}(s))</latex> whenever <latex>v</latex> and <latex>s</latex> denote the
  same language, because both route through the //same//
  augmentation pipeline. It is **not** claimed that a v1
  fingerprint is preserved across the v2 migration — see
  §VI.3 and §XIII.2. What makes v1 and v2 tags non-confusable
  is the version digit's **fixed offset** (tag index 30),
  not the fingerprint's length (§IX.2.2).
end note

== 4. Registration — the VALUE is what is stored ==
FP -> REG : ""insertVersion(ret, &#34;lib&#34;, deployer, id, ver, v)""
REG --> P : <latex>\texttt{rho:lib:1.*:}\langle\mathit{pk}\rangle\texttt{:}\langle\mathit{id}\rangle\texttt{:}\langle\mathit{ver}\rangle</latex>

== 5. Retrieval and installation — the gates run AGAIN ==
P -> REG : fetch by registry URI
REG --> P : the specification **value** <latex>v'</latex>\n(//not// a ""LanguageDef"": the registry stores data)
P -> E : <latex>\mathcal{E}(v')</latex> — **G1 and G2 re-run on the retrieved value**
note right of E #A7F3D0
  There is **no shortcut** from the registry to the backends.
  A retrieved specification is an ordinary untrusted value and
  re-enters the same fail-closed door as a locally constructed
  one. This is the whole point of §IX: the adversarial input
  arrives here.
end note
E -> VAL : <latex>\texttt{LanguageDef}</latex>
VAL -> BE : validated, augmented <latex>\texttt{LanguageDef}</latex>
BE -> RS : <latex>\texttt{rhoapi::Par}</latex> driver network,\nset-automaton pattern DAG
BE -> RS : reflected head tags <latex>\ulcorner \mathcal{F}\cdot L \urcorner</latex>

== 6. Use ==
P -> RS : FLT ""L`term`"" resolved by <latex>\mathcal{F}</latex>
RS --> P : reduced reflected term

legend right
  |= Colour |= Concept (pinned palette, diagrams/PALETTE.md) |
  |<#E0E7FF> | **P3** Rholang value path |
  |<#A7F3D0> | **P9** Fail-closed gate |
  |<#FBCFE8> | **P10** Unforgeable identity |
  |<#DDD6FE> | **P11** Registry-resolved reference |
  |<#DCFCE7> | **P5** Generator emitting installable DATA |
  |<#BFDBFE> | **P8** Runtime substrate |
endlegend
@enduml
